From 85dd3f271e5598f521c3386fb4d86e93f3019367 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patch-author <a@a.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 06:40:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Patch 0374: fix early-Hatchery-access nav bug, wire up
 Founder's Pack grant

- MenuWindow.tsx: requestTab/consumeRequestedTab now validated against
  isTabVisible at both consumption points (initial mount, live-update
  effect) before switching -- closes a real playtester-reported bug
  where a notification's 'Go to Hatchery' button could open the panel
  before hatcheryUnlocked was ever true.
- pets.ts/PetManager.ts: pickHatchedPetDefId now takes an optional pool
  (default: base PETS, so existing callers are unaffected);
  PetManager.hatch passes DlcManager.allPets() so a dedicated DLC pet id
  actually resolves instead of silently falling through to a random
  base-roster pick.
- tools/import_pets.py: new RUBY_DRAGONLING spec (base_recolor to a
  ruby/amber palette), in a new DLC_PETS list kept OUT of the default
  PETS target list -- a plain run can never leak DLC art into the base
  game's own public/pets output; needs explicit --only ruby_dragonling.
  Grant rarity picked as 'common' only after generating and visually
  checking every tier -- higher tiers hue-shift away from ruby entirely.
- New public/dlc/founders_pack/pack.json (real DlcPackManifest, Ruby
  Dragonling PetDef). .gitignore excludes public/dlc/*/*/ (sprite art)
  while pack.json itself stays tracked.
- DlcManager.ts: FOUNDER_PACK_ID registered in KNOWN_DLC_PACKS.
- engine.ts: new GameEngine.grantFounderPackContentIfOwned, chained onto
  DlcManager.loadInstalledPacks(). One-time via new founderPackGranted
  flag (SAVE_VERSION 68->69). Grants a common-rarity Ruby Dragonling egg
  + 'The Founding Flame' guild title; deliberately never touches
  hatcheryUnlocked, relying on the nav fix above to keep the Hatchery
  panel unreachable until the real unlock quest completes.
- Verified: tsc --noEmit, vite build, electron-builder --linux dir
  package build, an 8-check runtime script (tsx) covering the DLC-pool
  resolution fix and the full grant simulation, and a real HTTP fetch of
  pack.json against the actual built dist output.
